                           Weizmann Institute of Science
                                 VM Tools Tape
                           -----------------------------


Below is a list of tools for your VM system.  Each number represents
another file on this tape.  Example: the 4th file on this tape
contains all the stuff needed to run APLOCKS.

1)  Documentation -
    WICC     MEMO
    WICC     DOC     (this listing)

2)  ENABLE/DISABLE EXECS - These two execs enhance the capabality of
    the ENABLE and DISABLE commands to accept a range, i.e.
    EN 380-38F.  No CP or CMS modifications needed.
    ENABLE   EXEC
    DISABLE  EXEC

3)  STORAGE - An assembler program to display a better indication of
    CP storage utilization.  The CP IND "STORAGE-nnn%" only indicates
    what percentage of storage is being utilizied by in-queue users.
    This sometimes is not quite enough.  This program will loop
    through all VMBLOKs and add up the total number of resident pages
    at the present time.  This gives a better indication of what
    percentage of storage is in use.  No CP or CMS modifications
    needed.
    The STORAGE EXEC serves as an example of how to call STORAGE
    and have the results displayed in a pseudo fullscreen mode via
    IPF's WAKEUP and CLRSCRN.  STORAGE can be called directly if you
    do not have these modules.
    Class E privileges required.
    STORAGE  ASSEMBLE
    STORAGE  MODULE
    STORAGE  EXEC

4)  APLOCKS - An assembler program to display the current status of
    all AP/MP locks (i.e. real storage, I/O, etc.).  A recommended
    CP modification is included in the comments in order to get
    the full extent of locks.  This CP modification is not required.
    Class E privileges required.
    APLOCKS  ASSEMBLE
    APLOCKS  MODULE

5)  MAXUSERS - An assembler program to set and display the number of
    maximum users allowed onto VM at one time.  Requires CP
    modifications.  Requires class E privileges.
    MAXUSERS ASSEMBLE
    MAXUSERS MODULE
    DMKEMA   MAXUSERS
    DMKLOG   MAXUSERS
    DMKLOH   MAXUSERS

6)  TAPSENSE - An assembler program to return sense information about a
    tape drive.  Excellent for debugging problem tape drives.
    TAPSENSE ASSEMBLE
    TAPSENSE MODULE

7)  FBASENSE - An assembler program to return sense information about
    any FBA device.
    FBASENSE ASSEMBLE
    FBASENSE MODULE

8)  SEG - An assembler program to either load, load nonshared, find
    or purge any segment defined in DMKSNT.  Invaluable for debugging
    DMKSNT problems and segment overlaps.
    SEG      ASSEMBLE
    SEG      MODULE

9)  CALC - An XEDIT and EXEC macro to allow desktop calculations from
    within XEDIT.  Supports nested parentheses, + - / * and **.
    Free format syntax.  No real numbers supported (i.e. 1.4).
    CALC     XEDIT
    CALC     EXEC

10) TBROWSE - A utility exists for full screen scanning of disk files
    (BROWSE), for full screen scanning of virtual reader files (PEEK),
    and now a utility exists for full screen examination of files that
    reside on tape.  File #11 must be loaded in order to reassemble
    TBROWSE.  WISMAC must be included in GLOBAL MACLIB, and FORTSUB
    must be included in GLOBAL TXTLIB when doing the LOAD.
    TBROWSE  ASSEMBLE  (packed format)
    TBROWSE  MODULE
    TBROWSE  HELPCMSL

11) MACROS - This section contains all the support code for running
    full screen applications.
    WISMAC   MACLIB    (required for reassembly of various modules)
    FORTSUB  TXTLIB    (required for LOAD of various modules)
    FORTSUB  MEMO      (explanation of what exists in FORTSUB)
    SCREEN   ASSEMBLE  (packed format)

12) SNAKE - A full screen game.  WISMAC must be included in GLOBAL
    MACLIB in order to reassemble.
    SNAKE    ASSEMBLE  (packed format)
    SNAKE    MODULE
    SNAKE    HELPGAME

13) SLASH - A full screen real-time game.  WISMAC must be included
    in GLOBAL MACLIB in order ro reassemble (file #12) and FORTSUB
    must be included in GLOBAL TXTLIB when doing a LOAD.
    SLASH    ASSEMBLE  (packed format)
    SLASH    MODULE
    SLASH    HELPGAME

14) EMSG - An assembler subroutine to format message text according
    to the receipent's EMSG setting instead of the sender's.  Requires
    either class E or C.  EMSGTEST is an example of a call to EMSG.
    EMSG     ASSEMBLE
    EMSGTEST ASSEMBLE

15) FORCE - An EXEC file that improves the FORCE command to accept
    the syntax of 'FORCE ALL EXCEPT userid1 userid2 ... useridn'.
    FORCE    EXEC
